{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1218630-clarification-of-biokenesis-supernatural-merit","id":1218630,"title":"Clarification of Biokenesis Supernatural Merit","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-14T11:46:43-07:00","id":1218630,"title":"Clarification of Biokenesis Supernatural Merit","content":"The biokenesis supernatural merit is vague and possibly in need of some more elaboration. I was wondering if it even needs errata, but maybe I'm just nitpicking?<br /> <br /> Aside from Biokenesis' normal power to shift dots of physical attributes around, it also halves all healing times for the owner of the merit. My question is &quot;at what dot does a character gain this halved healing time benefit?&quot; <br /> <br /> <br /> Do I only need one dot to benefit? Should the healing times be linked to other dots of the merit? (e.g. five dots allows you to heal a point of bashing in 5 minutes, a point of lethal in ... etc)<br /> <br /> <br /> I apologise of this has been ansked before, but I couldn't find any relevant post or information about my specific question. <br /> <br /> (I'm on mobile; please forgive any formatting issues)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24230-maddasher","name":"MadDasher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T11:52:55-07:00","id":1218633,"title":"","content":"The dot rating only changes the number of dots that can be shifted. If you have Biokinesis, regardless of dot rating, you receive the halved healing time benefit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.